[2026-07-08T01:20:31+08:00][sql] INSERT INTO `ai_dev_run_logs` SET `run_id` = 13 , `seq` = 23 , `event_type` = 'assistant' , `content` = '{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"81c30682-e2bd-4228-b127-c6832fdfef3d\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-pro\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile my review findings.\\n\\nSummary of all issues:\\n\\n**Blocking Issues:**\\n\\n1. **`is_int()` rejects string integers from form-encoded POST requests** (BubbleSort.php:41 in validate): When the API receives form-encoded data (`nums[]=5&nums[]=3`), PHP casts array elements as strings. `is_int(\'5\')` returns `false`, causing valid integer inputs to be rejected. This is a correctness bug — the requirement says the API should accept integer arrays, but it silently rejects valid integer values sent via standard form encoding. Project\'s own convention uses `\\/d` modifier and `intval()` (see Test.php) to handle this. Should use `is_numeric($v) && $v == (int)$v` or `filter_var($v, FILTER_VALIDATE_INT) !== false`.\\n\\n2. **`$this->error($validate->getError())` does not pass the actual error code** (BubbleSort.php:29): `getError()` returns a message string like `\\\"160006,nums\\\"` in this codebase convention. The `error()` method\'s third parameter `$code` defaults to 10001. The `result()` method then sets `errno` to 10001 instead of the intended 160006. This means the API response\'s `errno` field is always 10001 for validation failures, while the actual error code is embedded only in the `msg` field as text. While the existing project codebase uses this same pattern (see ChooseSchool.php which also returns error codes as message strings), this is still a design flaw that makes structured error handling impossible for API consumers.\\n\\nWait, actually looking at this more carefully in the context of this codebase... Looking at how `ComErrorDescs::errmsg()` works:\\n\\n```php\\nif (false !== strpos($errcode, \',\')) {\\n    list($errcode, $repMsg) = explode(\',\', $errcode);\\n}\\n```\\n\\nSo the convention is to pass `\\\"160006,paramName\\\"` as the message. The `errmsg()` function parses this and formats it. But who calls `errmsg()`? Looking at the code, it seems like `errmsg()` is meant to be called when constructing error responses. But in the controller, `$this->error($validate->getError())` directly passes the raw message string without going through `errmsg()`.\\n\\nActually wait - does TP5\'s validate somehow use `errmsg()`? Let me think... No, TP5\'s validate `getError()` just returns the raw string value from `$message`. So the error message would be the literal string `\\\"160006,nums\\\"`.\\n\\nThen `$this->error(\\\"160006,nums\\\")` sets `$msg = \\\"160006,nums\\\"` and `$code = 10001`.\\n\\nIn `result()`, the output is:\\n```json\\n{\\\"errno\\\": 10001, \\\"success\\\": 10001, \\\"data\\\": [], \\\"msg\\\": \\\"160006,nums\\\"}\\n```\\n\\nThis is problematic. But looking at other code, `$this->error(\\\"参数错误【school_major_id】\\\")` in AppMajor also doesn\'t pass a proper error code. So this is an existing codebase pattern issue, not specific to this PR.\\n\\nHowever, it IS a real issue for this new API. Let me decide if it\'s blocking or warning.\\n\\nI think issue #1 (is_int) is definitely blocking - it\'s a correctness bug.\\nIssue #2 (error code) - I\'ll flag as a warning since it follows the project\'s existing (flawed) pattern.\\n\\n**Warnings:**\\n\\n1. Error code not properly passed: validation error codes embedded in msg string, errno always 10001\\n2. No array size limit (plan mentions risk of O(n²) timeout for large arrays)\\n3. Error message labels use English field name \'nums\' instead of Chinese description, inconsistent with existing ChooseSchool conventions (which use Chinese like \'当前状态\')\\n\\n**Suggestions:**\\n\\n1. Add `max:1000` or similar array size limit in validation rules\\n2. Use `filter_var` or `is_numeric` instead of `is_int` for broader compatibility\\n3. Use Chinese parameter name labels for error messages\\n4. Pass actual error codes explicitly as third argument to `$this->error()`\\n\\nLet me finalize the JSON.\",\"signature\":\"81c30682-e2bd-4228-b127-c6832fdfef3d\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1056,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":41984,\"output_tokens\":0,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"aa7bff69-ed3b-4666-90cb-dfd288bf0ecb\",\"uuid\":\"8172faa6-1bf2-42be-93db-31909dacf3ee\"}' , `created_at` = '2026-07-08 01:20:31' [ RunTime:0.001970s ]
