[\'nums\' => $nums])) {\\n    $errorRaw = $validate->getError();\\n    \\/\\/ Parse error code from raw error message (format: \\\"errorCode,label\\\")\\n    $errorCode = 160002; \\/\\/ EC_UNKNOWN fallback\\n    if (strpos($errorRaw, \',\') !== false) {\\n        list($codeStr, ) = explode(\',\', $errorRaw, 2);\\n        $errorCode = (int)$codeStr;\\n    }\\n    $errorMsg = \\\\app\\\\api\\\\library\\\\ComErrorDescs::errmsg($errorRaw);\\n    $this->error($errorMsg, [], $errorCode);\\n}\\n```\\n\\nWait, but the `$validate->getError()` returns the first error message. The `$message` array format is `\'nums.require\' => ComErrorDescs::EC_MISSING_PARAM . \',\' . \'整数数组\'` which evaluates to `\'160006,整数数组\'`.\\n\\nSo `$validate->getError()` returns `\'160006,整数数组\'`.\\n\\nThen I can parse it. Let me also use `ComErrorDescs::errmsg()` to convert it to a human-readable message, but wait — looking at the existing flow:\\n\\nWhen `$this->error($msg)` is called, it calls `$this->result($msg, $data, $code)`, which directly uses `$msg` as the message. If I pass the raw `\'160006,整数数组\'` as msg, it would show that raw string. That\'s not good.\\n\\nBut looking at how other controllers handle it (like the User.php), they just pass human-readable messages like `$msg = \'subj_no\'` and set `$errno` separately.\\n\\nWait, I think the issue is that the current code passes the raw validator error (which is the error code + label string) directly as the message to `$this->error()`. Let me trace the flow:\\n\\n1. Validator\'s `$message` is: `\'nums.require\' => \'160006,整数数组\'`\\n2. When validation fails, `$validate->getError()` returns `\'160006,整数数组\'`\\n3. Controller does `$this->error(\'160006,整数数组\')`\\n4. `ApiAuth::error()` calls `ApiAuth::result(\'160006,整数数组\', [], 10001)` (default code)\\n5. Response: `{\\\"errno\\\": 10001, \\\"msg\\\": \\\"160006,整数数组\\\", ...}`\\n\\nThis is NOT the right format — the error code is wrong (always 10001) and the message is the raw code+label.\\n\\nThe review feedback says to fix this by extracting the error code and using `ComErrorDescs::errmsg()` to format the message. Let me implement this properly:\\n\\n```php\\nif (!$validate->scene(\'sort\')->check([\'nums\' => $nums])) {\\n    $errorRaw = $validate->getError();\\n    $errorCode = 160002; \\/\\/ EC_UNKNOWN as default\\n    if (strpos($errorRaw, \',\') !== false) {\\n        list($codeStr, ) = explode(\',\', $errorRaw, 2);\\n        $errorCode = (int)$codeStr;\\n    }\\n    $errorMsg = \\\\app\\\\api\\\\library\\\\ComErrorDescs::errmsg($errorRaw);\\n    $this->error($errorMsg, [], $errorCode);\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThis would produce:\\n- $errorMsg = \\\"缺少参数 [整数数组]\\\" (via ComErrorDescs::errmsg\'s sprintf)\\n- $errorCode = 160006\\n- Response: `{\\\"errno\\\": 160006, \\\"msg\\\": \\\"缺少参数 [整数数组]\\\", ...}`\\n\\nThat\'s the correct behavior.\\n\\nNow let me implement all changes.\",\"signature\":\"e641622a-ece6-4ac4-9f76-0655c110cf95\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":339,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":40704,\"output_tokens\":0,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"34f52b2e-9dc4-4d58-b197-6c67c9956f04\",\"uuid\":\"a7892d60-3896-4f7c-b936-37192f86913f\"}' , `created_at` = '2026-07-08 01:22:52' [ RunTime:0.001280s ]
