{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"e641622a-ece6-4ac4-9f76-0655c110cf95\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-pro\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"They use `$this->result($msg, $data, $errno)`. Now I have a good understanding of the patterns.\\n\\nNow let me implement all the changes. Here\'s my plan:\\n\\n**1. 验证器 `BubbleSort.php`:**\\n- Change `\'nums\'` to `\'整数数组\'` in all error messages\\n- Add `checkMaxLength` custom validation method (max 1000)\\n- Add the new rule to the `$rule` array\\n\\n**2. 控制器 `BubbleSort.php`:**\\n- Split validation error to extract error code and pass as third parameter to `$this->error()`\\n- Use `ComErrorDescs::errmsg()` to format the error message\\n\\n**3. 逻辑层 `BubbleSort.php`:**\\n- Add early return for empty array\\n\\n**4. 路由 `route.php`:**\\n- Already has the route added. No changes needed.\\n\\nLet me now write the updated files. Let me start with the validator.\\n\\nFor the validator, I need to decide on the approach:\\n- Keep `checkNotEmptyArray` which checks non-empty and all elements are integers\\n- Add `checkMaxLength` to check array length <= 1000\\n- Add it to the rule: `\'nums\' => \'require|array|checkNotEmptyArray|checkMaxLength\'`\\n\\nFor the error message on `checkMaxLength`, I\'ll use `EC_INVALID_PARAM` since a too-large array is an invalid parameter.\\n\\nWait, actually let me reconsider the approach. The `checkNotEmptyArray` method currently checks both non-empty AND element types. If I add `checkMaxLength` separately, it\'s cleaner. But I could also integrate the max length check into `checkNotEmptyArray`. I\'ll keep them separate for clarity since the review specifically asked for it.\\n\\nNow, let me write the code.\\n\\nFor the controller, the key change is:\\n```php\\nif (!$validate->scene(\'sort\')->check([\'nums\' => $nums])) {\\n    $errorRaw = $validate->getError();\\n    // Parse error code from raw error message (format: \\\"errorCode,label\\\")\\n    $errorCode = 160002; // EC_UNKNOWN fallback\\n    if (strpos($errorRaw, \',\') !== false) {\\n        list($codeStr, ) = explode(\',\', $errorRaw, 2);\\n        $errorCode = (int)$codeStr;\\n    }\\n    $errorMsg = \\\\app\\\\api\\\\library\\\\ComErrorDescs::errmsg($errorRaw);\\n    $this->error($errorMsg, [], $errorCode);\\n}\\n```\\n\\nWait, but the `$validate->getError()` returns the first error message. The `$message` array format is `\'nums.require\' => ComErrorDescs::EC_MISSING_PARAM . \',\' . \'整数数组\'` which evaluates to `\'160006,整数数组\'`.\\n\\nSo `$validate->getError()` returns `\'160006,整数数组\'`.\\n\\nThen I can parse it. Let me also use `ComErrorDescs::errmsg()` to convert it to a human-readable message, but wait — looking at the existing flow:\\n\\nWhen `$this->error($msg)` is called, it calls `$this->result($msg, $data, $code)`, which directly uses `$msg` as the message. If I pass the raw `\'160006,整数数组\'` as msg, it would show that raw string. That\'s not good.\\n\\nBut looking at how other controllers handle it (like the User.php), they just pass human-readable messages like `$msg = \'subj_no\'` and set `$errno` separately.\\n\\nWait, I think the issue is that the current code passes the raw validator error (which is the error code + label string) directly as the message to `$this->error()`. Let me trace the flow:\\n\\n1. Validator\'s `$message` is: `\'nums.require\' => \'160006,整数数组\'`\\n2. When validation fails, `$validate->getError()` returns `\'160006,整数数组\'`\\n3. Controller does `$this->error(\'160006,整数数组\')`\\n4. `ApiAuth::error()` calls `ApiAuth::result(\'160006,整数数组\', [], 10001)` (default code)\\n5. Response: `{\\\"errno\\\": 10001, \\\"msg\\\": \\\"160006,整数数组\\\", ...}`\\n\\nThis is NOT the right format — the error code is wrong (always 10001) and the message is the raw code+label.\\n\\nThe review feedback says to fix this by extracting the error code and using `ComErrorDescs::errmsg()` to format the message. Let me implement this properly:\\n\\n```php\\nif (!$validate->scene(\'sort\')->check([\'nums\' => $nums])) {\\n    $errorRaw = $validate->getError();\\n    $errorCode = 160002; // EC_UNKNOWN as default\\n    if (strpos($errorRaw, \',\') !== false) {\\n        list($codeStr, ) = explode(\',\', $errorRaw, 2);\\n        $errorCode = (int)$codeStr;\\n    }\\n    $errorMsg = \\\\app\\\\api\\\\library\\\\ComErrorDescs::errmsg($errorRaw);\\n    $this->error($errorMsg, [], $errorCode);\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThis would produce:\\n- $errorMsg = \\\"缺少参数 [整数数组]\\\" (via ComErrorDescs::errmsg\'s sprintf)\\n- $errorCode = 160006\\n- Response: `{\\\"errno\\\": 160006, \\\"msg\\\": \\\"缺少参数 [整数数组]\\\", ...}`\\n\\nThat\'s the correct behavior.\\n\\nNow let me implement all changes.\",\"signature\":\"e641622a-ece6-4ac4-9f76-0655c110cf95\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":339,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":40704,\"output_tokens\":0,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"34f52b2e-9dc4-4d58-b197-6c67c9956f04\",\"uuid\":\"a7892d60-3896-4f7c-b936-37192f86913f\"}
